re parsing deeply nested arrays can recurse without limit. Versions 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 both fix it.\n- **Version choice:** I first went with 2.9.4 because it was the smaller jump, but the approver turned that commit down. They asked for 3.1.0, since the team finished moving to fastjson 3.x last sprint, so I used that.\n- **Changes:** On branch `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, `requirements.txt` now pins `fastjson==3.1.0`, and I added a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 597dec07c7.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe branch name still says 2.9.4 because I created it before the version changed, but it contains 3.1.0. The PR description notes this. The PR hasn't been merged: merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}